{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["What business do you have sitting here, and who do you have here from a family that could help you?" "<b>That you have hewn yourself a tomb here.</b> Like כרית, and <small>(Deuteronomy 6:11)</small> “hewn cisterns,” and the meaning is that you think in your heart that you will be steward forever, and that you will die in Jerusalem, and you have already prepared a grave for yourself there. And the one who says the meaning of קבר is like “palace” is not correct — and the proof is “you will die there.”"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:41.646879865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}